    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so they're basically just like a middleman to keep everything fair. is there a reason it has to be a separate person/company though? like why can't the seller just hold the funds or something? seems like a lot of extra steps.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The separate entity maintains impartiality, preventing potential conflicts of interest that could arise if one of the parties held the funds. If the seller held the money, they could potentially misuse it or refuse to release it if they changed their mind. Using a dedicated escrow agent ensures that the money is only released once *all* contractual obligations, like the title transfer, have been satisfied.",
