      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow accounts are legally protected trust accounts, which significantly mitigates the risk of funds being lost. In most states, these funds are held in a segregated account separate from the escrow company's operating money. While no system is completely risk-free, the fiduciary duties placed on escrow agents are strict, and state regulations heavily govern the handling of those client funds.",
